    <string name="setup_intro_how">Sunloom changes your wallpaper by itself: bright pictures by day, dark ones at night.</string>
    <string name="setup_intro_sources">The pictures are free to use and safe for work. They come from Wikimedia Commons Featured Pictures and the open collections of the Art Institute of Chicago, the Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Cleveland Museum of Art and the National Gallery of Denmark.</string>
    <string name="setup_intro_network">It downloads new pictures only on a network that is not metered, like home Wi-Fi, and keeps working after you close it.</string>
    <string name="setup_intro_privacy">Nothing about you leaves your device: no account, no ads, no tracking.</string>
    <string name="setup_nasa_note">NASA\'s photo library is off by default, because many of its pictures are charts, diagrams and event photos rather than wallpapers. You can turn it on in Sources.</string>
